AUDIO: 'is that I liked having it further back on my desk, but that means that when I pulled it down, it was several inches away from the edge of my desk. So, I ended up pulling the monitor a little closer to my head than I normally would with a monitor like this, so that it was'

[11:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just easier to pull down to the drawing position. And when I did that, I did notice kind of the blurriness of the text more than I normally would on a monitor. Another thing it has here is a matte coating that is very good for'

[11:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'drawing because it gives it a little bit of texture. So, when a pen is going over it, it doesn\'t float around like it does on a lot of glossy screens. It also reduces glare, which a lot of people like on a design monitor. But not all matte coatings are made equal, and this'

[11:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is one of the grainier coatings out there. So, when you have that lower resolution of the display matched with this particular matte coating, it can make that text look less than crisp. Again, on a on a cheaper monitor, this'

[11:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wouldn\'t be such a big deal. But on the second most expensive display I\'ve ever reviewed, I I really want my text to pop. The color range on this monitor is pretty solid. I found the accuracy to be good enough. Uh, it\'s not going to be'

[11:59] [scene:talking_head]
VISUAL: The reviewer is speaking directly to the camera.
AUDIO: 'the Apple Studio Display or one of those BenQ Design monitors. It\'s not going to be that good, but it\'s plenty good for what I need it for. It\'s got a 90% Adobe RGB coverage, 94% DCI P3 coverage. Another thing I noticed after using it'

[12:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for a few days was there was some color bleed along the bottom of the display. It took me a while to notice. It wasn\'t like super pronounced, and it\'s one of those things that I didn\'t pick up on early on. And I think the reason why is because when the monitor is on for a'

[12:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'long time is when I start to notice it. So when I just toggle it on for the first time, you don\'t see it at all. And for most of the time that I was using this, I was in Windows. Windows has a gray taskbar along the bottom. So on a lighter screen, you don\'t notice the'

[12:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'light bleed quite as much. But when I would move it over to my Mac and play with it there, Photoshop has a darker interface. So when I was in Photoshop, that\'s when I could really see it because that black was lined up along the bottom where that light bleed was.'

[12:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is a pen enabled touchcreen. Usually on a monitor, that\'s not something I\'m looking for, but since you can pull this down and draw on it, it\'s a great addition and it works really well. It\'s worth noting that the touch works on both Mac and PCs. The monitor'

[13:02] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A hand continues drawing on the ALOGIC monitor with a stylus.
AUDIO: 'does come with a lot of bells and whistles here that you find on some of the highest end displays out there. For example, there is a ton of ports on the back of this inputs for HDMI, USBC, display port. There\'s a second display port here, so you can use it to like'

[13:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'daisy chain another monitor to this monitor, at least if you\'re using it on Windows. There are two USBA ports for plugging in accessories. There\'s two, three USB type-C ports for that. Although one\'s at like the very tippy'

[13:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'top of the monitor, that\'s probably for people who want to use light bars and like plug them directly in there using those USB ports along the side, whether it\'s the A or the C. You can charge up to 90 watts out of those. So, you could'

[13:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even get fast charging out of this monitor. If you have a Mac laptop and you plug it into this monitor to use it as a monitor, it\'s also going to charge up your MacBook. It\'ll probably do the same thing to a Windows laptop. I just don\'t have one sitting around to test.'

[13:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There is an audio jack. Uh there\'s an Ethernet port. There are these magnetic little cable clips that like snap into the side. That\'s a nice touch to kind of keep your cords clean. There are onboard speakers here. They\'re they\'re kind of'

